31.For the purpose of carrying out its objects, theAuthority shall, perform and discharge all or any of thefollowing duties and functions:–

(a)direct controllers to comply with the provisions ofsections 11 and 13 in accordance with theinformation set out in Schedule V hereto;

(b)monitor and examine all data processing operationsto ensure the due compliance by controllers orprocessors, of the obligations imposed on suchcontrollers or processors under this Act, either ofits own motion or at the request of a data subject;

(c)issue directives to any specific controller orprocessor regarding any processing activityperformed by such controller or processor;

(d)facilitate or undertake training, based oninternational best practices, for controllers andprocessors to ensure the effective implementationof the provisions of this Act;

(e)issue directives to ensure effective implementationof data protection management programmes by thecontrollers;

(f)promote transparency and self-regulation amongcontrollers and processors;

(d)facilitate or undertake training, based oninternational best practices, for controllers andprocessors to ensure the effective implementationof the provisions of this Act;

(e)issue directives to ensure effective implementationof data protection management programmes by thecontrollers;

(f)promote transparency and self-regulation amongcontrollers and processors;

(h)recommend to the Government on all mattersrelating to data protection;

(i)represent the Government internationally onmatters relating to data protection with the approvalof the Minister;

